187/259/307  further A logout/relogin cycles (with "Remember me?" toggled
             on the later ones) -- 192/196/263/268/311 all moduleId=null
             immediately post-login, NEVER a stale foreign value; 213/216/
             284/285/316 correctly settle back to A's own moduleId=2 once
             zone+module state resolves (either via re-selection or, once
             userNumber persists, via the identity-scoped cache).

VERDICT (AC1): across 4 login/logout account-switch cycles (A->B->A->A->A),
zero cross-user moduleId bleed observed on cart/list. Every "wrong" value
observed was the CURRENT account's own null/absent state, never the
previous account's stale id. This is the exact defect NEARS-2490 fixed
(CartRepository._getCartDataOnline reading ModuleController._cacheModule,
an in-memory field never refreshed across a login/logout identity switch)
-- confirmed live, matching prior FAIL repro's methodology exactly.

OBSERVATION (AC2, quick spot-check, non-blocking): on several of the A
relogin cycles, the FIRST 1-2 cart/list calls post-login showed moduleId=
null even though A's own identity-scoped cache (cacheModuleId::u:
customer@nears.com) was confirmed present on-device (SharedPreferences
dump, id=2) from an earlier session. zoneId was ALSO <absent> on those
same early calls, and flutter.6ammart_user_number was observed to commit
to the on-device SharedPreferences store a few seconds AFTER login
returned 200, not synchronously with it -- consistent with an early-post-
login timing window before zone+identity state settles, not a resolution-
logic defect. This diff (cart_repository.dart) does not touch userNumber/
remember-me persistence or login timing/ordering at all -- the same race
would exist identically with the OLD code path (ModuleHelper.getCacheModule()
is populated on an equally async schedule). Flagged as a regression-
candidate followup, not a task_bug against this fix, and not a re-open of
AC2 (which has independent same-day evidence, ac2-relogin-continuity-and-
handoff-fix.log, showing the mechanism working end-to-end with a different
account).
